sentences.l:
And him then in the fore-house he found sitting, where for him the yard
high had been built, in a place seen-from-all-sides,
fine and large, round-running;

and in each
fifty swine, ground-sleepers, were penned,
females, breeders;

for them kept-diminishing, eating them,
the godlike suitors, since sent-forth the swineherd
always, of the sleek fat hogs, the best of all;

and the others, then,
went off, one this way, one that, with swine they had gathered,
the three;

for, over a godlike lord lamenting and grieving,
I sit, and for others fat swine I raise
to eat;

for the way of servants is this,
always afraid, whenever lords hold sway,
the young ones.

to no one so great,
of heroic men, neither of the dark mainland
nor of Ithaca itself;
